# Continuous workflow orchestrator

Repositories using this workflow employ **chief agent** (coordination) above a **polling orchestrator** (queue). Parent agents spawn **chief first**; chief spawns **one pr-fix/babysit worker per open PR** and delegates orchestrator for queue coordination. This rule documents orchestrator policy when chief (or the user) invokes it directly.

## Session start

After orienting to the repo, if **any** of: dirty `git status`, open `gh pr list`, or recent subagent work in agent-transcripts — **spawn or resume chief** (not orchestrator directly) unless the user waived chief for this session:

```
Task tool: subagent_type=generalPurpose, run_in_background=true
Prompt: Follow .cursor/skills/chief-agent/SKILL.md — run one SCAN→LOCK CHECK→PLAN→DELEGATE cycle and report locks + queue. Spawn pr-fix per open PR; delegate orchestrator for queue/split/routing when needed.
```

Chief dedupes locks and assigns **one pr-fix/babysit worker per open PR**. **Manual orchestrator invoke** (`run workflow orchestrator`) may run orchestrator directly when chief is waived or chief already delegated this turn.

## After substantive subagent work

When a `Task` subagent returns after **implementation**, **docs**, **PR babysit**, or **orchestrator** cycle:

1. Spawn or resume **chief** (not orchestrator directly) unless chief is in flight or waived.
2. Chief re-scans, updates locks, spawns pr-fix per open PR, and delegates orchestrator for queue/split/routing per the chief skill.
3. When executing orchestrator yourself this turn (chief delegation or user invoke), follow `.cursor/skills/workflow-orchestrator/SKILL.md`.

## One PR per task (hard)

- **Do not** bundle unrelated feature areas, docs, and unrelated fixes in one PR.
- Partition by disjoint file sets.
- Meta orchestrator plumbing stays its own PR (`agent/workflow-orchestrator-*`).

## Manual invoke

User phrase: **"run workflow orchestrator"** — read `.cursor/skills/workflow-orchestrator/SKILL.md` and run a full cycle (chief may have already delegated).

## Hooks

`subagentStop` / `stop` may inject a follow-up via `.cursor/hooks/orchestrator-remind.mjs` (chief-first). Treat as signal to run **chief**, not as a substitute for `WORKFLOW.md`.

## Ship bar unchanged

Orchestrator coordinates the queue and ensures each open PR has a pr-fix worker; it does **not** waive `WORKFLOW.md` steps 5–7, bot wait, thread closure, or project verify.
